## Import and Setup

- Import `motion` from `"motion/react"` for React components
- Import `AnimatePresence` for exit animations
- Import `useAnimate` for imperative animations
- Import `useInView` for scroll-triggered animations
- Import `usePresence` for custom exit animations
- Use `LazyMotion` with `domAnimation` for bundle optimization

## Core Animation Components

- Use `motion.div` for basic element animations
- Use `motion.button` for interactive element animations
- Use `motion.span` for text animations
- Use `motion.svg` for SVG element animations
- Use `motion.path` for path animations
- Use `motion.ul` and `motion.li` for list animations
- Use `AnimatePresence` for exit animations

## TypeScript Integration

- Strongly type animation variants with interfaces
- Use `z.infer<typeof schema>` for variant type extraction
- Define custom animation types for complex animations
- Use generic constraints for reusable animation components
- Type motion values with `MotionValue<T>`
- Use `Custom` prop for dynamic variant data

## Performance Optimization

- Use `LazyMotion` with `domAnimation` for tree-shaking
- Use `useMotionValue` for performance-critical animations
- Use `useAnimate` for complex animation sequences
- Use `layout` prop sparingly for layout animations
- Use `viewport={{ once: true }}` for one-time scroll animations
- Use `transition={{ type: "tween" }}` for simple animations
- Use `transition={{ type: "spring" }}` for natural motion

## Animation Patterns

- Use `initial` and `animate` props for enter animations
- Use `exit` prop with `AnimatePresence` for exit animations
- Use `whileHover` and `whileTap` for gesture animations
- Use `whileInView` for scroll-triggered animations
- Use `variants` for reusable animation states
- Use `custom` prop for dynamic variant data
- Use `staggerChildren` for sequential child animations

## Variant Management

- Define variants as const objects for type safety
- Use descriptive variant names like `"visible"`, `"hidden"`
- Use `transition` within variants for orchestration
- Use `when: "beforeChildren"` for parent-first animations
- Use `when: "afterChildren"` for child-first animations
- Use `staggerChildren` for staggered animations
- Use `delayChildren` for delayed child animations

## Gesture Animations

- Use `whileHover={{ scale: 1.1 }}` for hover effects
- Use `whileTap={{ scale: 0.95 }}` for tap feedback
- Use `whileFocus` for focus state animations
- Use `whileDrag` for drag gesture animations
- Use `drag` prop for draggable elements
- Use `dragConstraints` for drag boundaries
- Use `dragElastic` for drag resistance

## Scroll Animations

- Use `whileInView={{ opacity: 1 }}` for fade-in effects
- Use `viewport={{ once: true }}` for one-time triggers
- Use `viewport={{ amount: 0.5 }}` for partial visibility
- Use `useInView` hook for custom scroll logic
- Use `useScroll` for scroll-linked animations
- Use `scrollYProgress` for scroll-based transforms
- Use `scrollXProgress` for horizontal scroll animations

## Exit Animations

- Wrap components with `AnimatePresence` for exit animations
- Use unique `key` props for proper exit tracking
- Use `exit` prop to define exit animation states
- Use `usePresence` for custom exit logic
- Use `safeToRemove()` after exit animation completes
- Use `layoutId` for shared element transitions
- Use `mode="wait"` for sequential exit animations

## Accessibility

- Use `useReducedMotion` to respect user preferences
- Provide alternative animations for reduced motion
- Use `prefers-reduced-motion` media query
- Ensure animations don't interfere with navigation
- Use appropriate ARIA attributes for animated elements
- Test animations with screen readers
- Provide fallbacks for animation failures

## Error Handling

- Use `try-catch` blocks for animation controls
- Handle animation cleanup in `useEffect` return
- Use `controls.stop()` to cancel animations
- Handle animation failures gracefully
- Provide fallback states for failed animations
- Log animation errors for debugging
- Use `safeParse` pattern for animation validation

## Advanced Patterns

- Use `useAnimate` for complex animation sequences
- Use `animate()` function for imperative animations
- Use `useMotionValue` for performance-critical values
- Use `useTransform` for derived motion values
- Use `useSpring` for spring-based animations
- Use `useScroll` for scroll-linked animations
- Use `useTime` for time-based animations

## Vite Integration

- Configure Vite for optimal Motion tree-shaking
- Use dynamic imports for heavy animation components
- Use `LazyMotion` for code splitting
- Optimize bundle size with `domAnimation` only
- Use environment variables for animation settings
- Configure build optimization for animation assets
- Use Vite's HMR for animation development

## Testing and Debugging

- Test animations in different browsers
- Test animations with different performance levels
- Use React DevTools for animation debugging
- Test animations with reduced motion preferences
- Use `console.log` for animation state debugging
- Test animations in different viewport sizes
- Use performance profiling for animation optimization

## Best Practices

- Keep animations under 300ms for UI feedback
- Use easing functions for natural motion
- Prefer transform animations over layout changes
- Use `will-change` CSS property sparingly
- Avoid animating `height` and `width` properties
- Use `transform` and `opacity` for performance
- Test animations on mobile devices
- Ensure animations enhance user experience
